! Tune histories from the fused program: every operation it claims the CPU's bits for, in one ring.
! Exact and matrix drifts, correctors, a thin MULT, exact correctors with no kick, kick quadrupoles
! and sextupoles of order 4 and 6 with offsets and tilts, one with LEFFECTIVE, a DQCOR, sticky tapered
! apertures, collimators, a scraper, a SPEEDBUMP, a MAXAMP, an RFCA with no voltage, and a marker and a
! monitor. The verify build stops if any particle's history differs from the CPU's.
! The exact correctors had kicks until 2026-11-11. With a kick the CPU takes atan(), sin(), asin(),
! cos() and tan() for each particle, which the device's library can round differently, so the program
! no longer claims those; search-frequency-map-program-tolerance has them. With no kick the CPU makes
! the corrector a drift.
DE: EDRIFT,L=0.04
DM: DRIF,L=0.04
HM: HKICK,L=0.02,KICK=1e-5
VM: VKICK,L=0.02,KICK=-1e-5
MU: MULT,ORDER=2,KNL=2e-4,TILT=0.03
EH: EHKICK,L=0.03,KICK=0,CALIBRATION=0.97,TILT=0.02
EV: EVKICK,L=0.03,KICK=0,CALIBRATION=1.03,TILT=-0.01
QF: KQUAD,L=0.10,K1=0.8,N_SLICES=2,INTEGRATION_ORDER=6,SYNCH_RAD=0,ISR=0,PITCH=1e-4,YAW=2e-4
QD: KQUAD,L=0.10,LEFFECTIVE=0.08,K1=-0.8,N_SLICES=2,INTEGRATION_ORDER=4,DX=1e-5,TILT=0.001
SX: KSEXT,L=0.08,K2=2,N_SLICES=2,INTEGRATION_ORDER=6,SYNCH_RAD=0,ISR=0,DY=1e-5
DQ: DQCOR,L=0.1,K1=0.3,N_SLICES=4,HKICK=1e-5,VKICK=-1e-5
TC: TAPERAPC,L=0.01,RSTART=0.006,REND=0.005,STICKY=1
TR: TAPERAPR,L=0.01,XSTART=0.005,XEND=0.0045,YSTART=0.004,&
 YEND=0.0035,STICKY=1
RC: RCOL,L=0.01,X_MAX=0.0045,Y_MAX=0.0035
EC: ECOL,L=0.01,X_MAX=0.0045,Y_MAX=0.0035,EXPONENT=2
SC: SCRAPER,POSITION=0.004,INSERT_FROM="+X"
SB: SPEEDBUMP,L=0.2,CHORD=0.2,HEIGHT=0.00501256,POSITION=0.0045,&
 INSERT_FROM="-x"
MA: MAXAMP,X_MAX=0.0045,Y_MAX=0.0035,ELLIPTICAL=1
RF: RFCA,VOLT=0,FREQ=352055035.3734189,PHASE=140.9568545815895,CHANGE_P0=0
MK: MARK
MO: MONI,L=0.05

RING: LINE=(TC,DE,HM,VM,MU,EH,EV,QF,SX,DM,QD,DQ,TR,DM,RC,EC,SC,SB,MA,RF,MK,MO)
